<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>SCIM on Sujith Quintelier</title><link>https://quintelier.dev/update_tags/scim/</link><description>Recent content in SCIM on Sujith Quintelier</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:19:58 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://quintelier.dev/update_tags/scim/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>github: SCIM user responses now include a profileUrl attribute</title><link>https://quintelier.dev/updates/scim-user-responses-now-include-a-profileurl-attribute/</link><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:19:58 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://quintelier.dev/updates/scim-user-responses-now-include-a-profileurl-attribute/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;GitHub SCIM user responses now include the RFC 7643 standard &lt;code&gt;profileUrl&lt;/code&gt; attribute. It returns the absolute URL of the GitHub account linked to the external identity.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-09-16-scim-user-responses-now-include-a-profileurl-attribute" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>